## Required Variables

Create a file named `terraform.tfvars` in the root deployment directory.

Example:

```hcl
# Google Cloud Organization ID
org_id = "123456789012"

# Billing Account ID
billing_account = "AAAAAA-BBBBBB-CCCCCC"

# Project Configuration
project_id   = "my-gcp-project"
project_name = "My GCP Project"

# Deployment Region
region = "us-central1"

# Existing project used for Terraform bootstrapping/state management
bootstrap_project = "terraform-bootstrap"

# GKE Node Configuration
machine_type = "e2-standard-2"

# Kubernetes Cluster Name
cluster_name = "sue-cluster"
```

### Variable Description

| Variable          | Description                                                 |
| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
| org_id            | Google Cloud Organization ID                                |
| billing_account   | Billing account used for project billing                    |
| project_id        | Google Cloud project ID                                     |
| project_name      | Display name of the GCP project                             |
| region            | GCP region where resources will be deployed                 |
| bootstrap_project | Existing project used for Terraform state and bootstrapping |
| machine_type      | Machine type for GKE nodes                                  |
| cluster_name      | Name of the Kubernetes cluster                              |

### Example Used During Testing

```hcl
project_id   = "sue-project-dev-6992"
project_name = "SUE Project Dev"

region = "us-south1"

machine_type = "e2-standard-2"

cluster_name = "sue-cluster"
```

> Do not commit real Organization IDs, Billing Account IDs, service account credentials, or other sensitive information to version control.

