# Verifying the Deployment

Check cluster nodes:

```bash
kubectl get nodes
```

Check KServe:

```bash
kubectl get pods -n kserve
```

Check deployed model:

```bash
kubectl get inferenceservice -n llm
```

Expected result:

```text
READY=True
```

Check pod status:

```bash
kubectl get pods -n llm
```

Expected result:

```text
1/1 Running
```

---

# Testing the Model

Port forward the service:

```bash
kubectl port-forward svc/tiny-llama-predictor 8080:80 -n llm
```

List available models:

```bash
curl http://localhost:8080/openai/v1/models
```

Expected output:

```json
{
  "models": ["tiny-llama"]
}
```

Run a test prompt:

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/openai/v1/chat/completions ^
-H "Content-Type: application/json" ^
-d "{\"model\":\"tiny-llama\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Explain Kubernetes in one sentence\"}]}"
```

